🐳 Task 7: Dockerizing a Static Web Application

 🎯 Objective
Containerize a simple static web app (HTML, CSS, JS) using Docker and Nginx.

 🧩 Steps I Performed
1. Created project files: `index.html`, `style.css`, `script.js`  
2. Wrote a Dockerfile using `nginx:alpine`  
3. Built the Docker image: `docker build -t hello-web-app .`  
4. Ran the container: `docker run -d -p 8080:80 hello-web-app`  
5. Verified the app in browser: `http://localhost:8080`

 🧪 Expected Outcome
- Static website is served inside Docker container  
- HTML, CSS, and JS all work correctly  
- Accessible on port 8080
